-- ind-c-tests-ambiguous.l4: assertions of MY reading that fail or refuse against the encoding, where I judge the
-- SOURCE to allow both readings.  Every assertion here was decided before the encoding was opened
-- (work/ind-c/expectations.md, H5, H8, I8, J5-J9).  None was edited to match the code.
-- Counted: 12 assertions (2 fail, 10 refuse).

§ `ind-c: ambiguities`

`draft` MEANS `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`
`taken` MEANS `the SimpLEX reading that the encoding takes`
`not barred` MEANS `regulation 4 does not bar the service`
`barred` MEANS `regulation 4 bars the service`

§§ `AMB-1 (H5, H8): which head of s.59 the draft's 284 prices (2 fail)`

-- The draft's 2(d) reads "for an application to receive a licence or to renew it, under section 5"; the text as made
-- reads (2(c)) "for receiving a licence or renewing it, under section 5".  My reading: one fee, the licence fee under
-- s.5, worded differently, so the draft prices the licence (284) and no separate application fee.  The encoding's
-- reading: two different heads of s.59 ("submitting an application" and "granting a licence"), so the draft prices
-- the application and is silent on the licence.  The words support the encoding at least as well as me.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `AMB-2 (I8): the draft's regulation 4, which the screenshot does not show (2 refuse)`

-- The SimpLEX panel itself says what the draft's reg 4 does ("reg 4: prohibits registration without payment").
-- My reading takes that statement as the draft's reg 4; the encoding refuses, the text of reg 4 not being visible.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `draft` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 272 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `draft` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 273 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY

